  // To do this, create a shape tensor for broadcasting.
  // Since StableHLO does not have explicit broadcast, we simulate broadcasting by reshaping and broadcasting.
  // But as per the constraints, we can use "stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim" if available.
  // Since not specified, we can simulate broadcasting via "stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim" operation.
  // For simplicity, assume "stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim" exists:
  // (Note: If not, one can generate a broadcasted tensor via multiple reshape and broadcast operations.)

  // Create shape attribute for broadcast: broadcast along dimensions 0 and 2, keep dimension 1 as is.
  // Input shape: [6,7,8]
  // Broadcast shape: [6,7,8]
  // The iota tensor shape: [7]
  // To broadcast to [6,7,8], we need to reshape iota to [1,7,1], then broadcast.

  // Step 2a: Reshape iota to [1,7,1]
  %iota_reshaped = "stablehlo.reshape"(%iota_tensor) {shape = dense< [1, 7, 1] > } : (tensor<7xi64>) -> tensor<1x7x1xi64>

  // Step 2b: Broadcast to [6,7,8]
